Engine-verified precedence of `|`, the error fallback. Every record here was
confirmed against a real client evaluator (QnA 11.x, macOS, 2026-08-30)
using probes whose outcome differs between the candidate parses -- see the
titles for the deciding answer. The model they pin: `|` binds between the
multiplicative class (`*`, `/`, `mod`, `&`) and `as`, the engine refuses an
unparenthesized multiplicative result as a `|` left operand, and `exists`
and `not` take their operand at the same level as `|` (so a trailing
fallback applies to the whole exists/not, and no comparison nests inside).

==== the fallback binds tighter than = (qna: 0 = exit code of action | 999 is False, not 999)
0 = exit code of action | 999
----
(bin "="
  (num "0")
  (bar (of (ref "exit code") (ref "action")) (num "999")))

==== the fallback binds tighter than = on the left too (qna: 1 | 0 = 0 is False)
1 | 0 = 0
----
(bin "=" (bar (num "1") (num "0")) (num "0"))

==== the fallback binds tighter than * on the left (qna: 1 | 2 * 3 is 3)
1 | 2 * 3
----
(bin "*" (bar (num "1") (num "2")) (num "3"))

==== the fallback binds tighter than + on the left (qna: 1 | 2 + 3 is 4)
1 | 2 + 3
----
(bin "+" (bar (num "1") (num "2")) (num "3"))

==== the fallback binds tighter than + on the right (qna: 2 + erroring | 5 is 7)
2 + 3 | 5
----
(bin "+" (num "2") (bar (num "3") (num "5")))

==== the fallback nests as the first factor of a product (qna: 2 + 3 | 5 * 2 is 8)
2 + 3 | 5 * 2
----
(bin "+"
  (num "2")
  (bin "*" (bar (num "3") (num "5")) (num "2")))

==== a trailing + applies to the fallback's result (qna: erroring | 999 + 1 is 1000)
exit code of action | 999 + 1
----
(bin "+"
  (bar (of (ref "exit code") (ref "action")) (num "999"))
  (num "1"))

==== the fallback binds tighter than or (qna: 1 or 2 | 3 demands a boolean, so 2 | 3 nested)
1 or 2 | 3
----
(bin "or" (num "1") (bar (num "2") (num "3")))

==== fallbacks chain (qna: 1 | 2 | 3 is 1)
1 | 2 | 3
----
(bar (bar (num "1") (num "2")) (num "3"))

==== a parenthesized product is a legal fallback left side (qna: (2 * 3) | 5 is 6)
(2 * 3) | 5
----
(bar (bin "*" (num "2") (num "3")) (num "5"))

==== a bare product cannot meet | (qna: parse error)
2 * 3 | 5
----
ERROR line 1 column 7

==== division cannot meet | either (qna: parse error)
2 / 4 | 5
----
ERROR line 1 column 7

==== mod cannot meet | either (qna: parse error)
10 mod 1 | 3
----
ERROR line 1 column 10

==== concatenation cannot meet | either (qna: parse error)
"a" & "b" | "c"
----
ERROR line 1 column 11

==== the refusal holds inside a sum (qna: 2 + 2 * 3 | 5 is a parse error)
2 + 2 * 3 | 5
----
ERROR line 1 column 11

==== exists does not absorb a fallback (qna: exists erroring | false is False, so the exists errored alone)
exists exit code of action | false
----
(bar (exists (of (ref "exit code") (ref "action"))) (ref "false"))

==== exists binds tighter than * (qna: exists 1 * 2 says operator times is not defined)
exists 1 * 2
----
(bin "*" (exists (num "1")) (num "2"))

==== a cast still nests inside exists (qna: exists 5 as string contains "T" says contains is not defined)
exists 5 as string
----
(exists (cast (num "5") "string"))

==== not binds tighter than = (qna: not 1 = 1 demands a boolean of the bare 1)
not 1 = 1
----
(bin "=" (un "not" (num "1")) (num "1"))

==== not does not absorb a fallback (qna: not (erroring = 0) | true is True)
not (exit code of action = 0) | true
----
(bar
  (un "not" (bin "=" (of (ref "exit code") (ref "action")) (num "0")))
  (ref "true"))

==== a cast still nests inside not (qna: not 5 as boolean fails on the cast, not on not 5)
not 5 as boolean
----
(un "not" (cast (num "5") "boolean"))

==== unary minus binds tighter than the fallback (qna: - erroring | 5 is 5)
- exit code of action | 5
----
(bar (un "-" (of (ref "exit code") (ref "action"))) (num "5"))
